v5temp: acceptance-targeted SA temperature (built 2026-07-29, validating).

Replaces (T0, cooling 0.9995, reheat) with one acceptance-rate target curve:
T seeds itself from the first worsening delta, then a proportional controller
T *= exp(GAIN*(accEma - target)), target = ACC0*(1 - progress/hcFrac), 0 past
hcFrac. ACC0=0.30, EMA_A=0.02, GAIN=0.05.

Motive (2026-07-30): cooling 0.9995 freezes T after ~20k iters = ~4% of a
real-TL run (P6 900s ~ 200k+ iters/arm) -- the legacy schedule was tuned in
the 1-core T60-T300 era, so at official TLs the anneal degenerates to
hill-climbing for most of the budget. Acceptance targeting keeps exploration
alive at ANY time budget by construction.
